; Mip chain — plan 08 sugar: two textures generated from level 0 by ordinary
; render passes, one step each.
;
; `(mip-chain …)` lowers to per-level texture views (a sampled view of N−1 and
; an attachment view of N), one linear sampler, one fullscreen module +
; pipeline for the texture's format, one bind group and one render pass per
; generated level, and one step-group with the authored name. Level 0 is an
; input: nothing renders into it. Scheduling is the frame's `:perform` and
; nothing else — there is no load-time or once-only channel.
;
; Two chains, two extent classes:
;   • `mipTex`  64×64   — power-of-two levels 32, 16, 8
;   • `npotTex` 100×100 — ordinary non-power-of-two extents 50, 25, 12
;
; Pixels (including that NPOT behavior) are slice 3. This fixture's golden
; trace pins the lowered resources and the ascending pass order;
; examples/mip_chain_hand.sjon is the same program written out in core forms.

(texture :name mipTex :size [64 64] :format rgba8unorm
  :mip-level-count 4
  :usage [texture-binding render-attachment])

(texture :name npotTex :size [100 100] :format rgba8unorm
  :mip-level-count 4
  :usage [texture-binding render-attachment])

(mip-chain :name fillMips :texture mipTex)
(mip-chain :name fillMipsNpot :texture npotTex)

(frame :name main :perform [fillMips fillMipsNpot])
